+# ---------------------------------------------------------
+# Coarse discipline tiers — the faculty divisions and the top-level
+# categories. Restored from v2.1.2, which declared all 46 as instances.
+#
+# These are not new terms. Every one of the 41 categories below already
+# appears in this file as the object of an `rdfs:subClassOf`, i.e. as the
+# parent of one or more leaf disciplines. What they lacked was an
+# `rdf:type`, and `sh:class pulse:DisciplineEnumeration` walks
+# `rdf:type/rdfs:subClassOf*` FROM the value node — so a node with no
+# `rdf:type` fails the constraint no matter how many children it has.
+# The effect was that every coarse discipline tag was a SHACL violation.
+#
+# Coarse tagging has to stay expressible: a general-purpose numerical
+# library really is `wd:Q395` (Mathematics) and nothing narrower, and
+# forcing leaf-only precision pushes annotators and agents into inventing
+# specificity they cannot support.
+# ---------------------------------------------------------
+
+# Faculty divisions (top tier). v2.1.2 hung these off wd:Q11862829
+# ("academic discipline"), which it never declared; that dangling parent is
+# dropped here rather than reproduced, since a tag of "academic discipline"
+# carries no signal.
+wd:Q7112556 a pulse:DisciplineEnumeration; skos:prefLabel "Applied sciences"@en .
+wd:Q816264 a pulse:DisciplineEnumeration; skos:prefLabel "Formal sciences"@en .
+wd:Q80083 a pulse:DisciplineEnumeration; skos:prefLabel "Humanities"@en .
+wd:Q7991 a pulse:DisciplineEnumeration; skos:prefLabel "Natural sciences"@en .
+wd:Q34749 a pulse:DisciplineEnumeration; skos:prefLabel "Social sciences"@en .
